From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FineWine
Subject: [PATCH] nsi: Wait for cancelled change notifications to complete.

NsiCancelChangeNotification (CancelIPChangeNotify) returned while the cancel
was still on its way through nsiproxy, so the request's final status was
written to the caller's OVERLAPPED afterwards. Chromium's network change
notifier (Qt5WebEngineCore and CEF in Endfield's process) frees the OVERLAPPED
right after cancelling, so the late STATUS_CANCELLED / 0 write corrupted
whatever reused that memory; in Endfield it zeroed a table pointer in a
GetAdaptersAddresses frame and the game crashed. On Windows the cancelled
request has completed by the time CancelIPChangeNotify returns.
---
--- a/dlls/nsi/nsi.c
+++ b/dlls/nsi/nsi.c
@@ -118,13 +118,22 @@ err:
 
 DWORD WINAPI NsiCancelChangeNotification( OVERLAPPED *ovr )
 {
-    DWORD err = ERROR_SUCCESS;
+    HANDLE device = get_nsi_device( TRUE );
+    DWORD err = ERROR_SUCCESS, len;
 
     TRACE( "%p.\n", ovr );
 
     if (!ovr) return ERROR_NOT_FOUND;
-    if (!CancelIoEx(  get_nsi_device( TRUE ), ovr ))
-        err = GetLastError();
+    if (!CancelIoEx( device, ovr ))
+        return GetLastError();
+
+    /* The cancel reaches nsiproxy asynchronously, so the request's final status is written to
+     * the OVERLAPPED some time after CancelIoEx returns. Callers such as Chromium free the
+     * OVERLAPPED as soon as CancelIPChangeNotify returns, and the late write then lands in
+     * whatever reuses that memory. Wait for it, as the request has finished by then on Windows. */
+    if (ovr->Internal == STATUS_PENDING && !GetOverlappedResultEx( device, ovr, &len, 5000, FALSE )
+        && GetLastError() == WAIT_TIMEOUT)
+        WARN( "cancelled request %p did not complete.\n", ovr );
 
     return err;
 }
